  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Covered Bridge Light",
    "description": "A square grey stone lighthouse on a rock out in the water, reached only along a covered bridge: a red roof on white columns, so the keeper crosses in the dry whatever the weather. Its lantern and windows light up after dark in World View. 30 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Rock** — two dark Block 2x2s side by side make a rock, 4 by 2, standing out of the water, with Rocks round its foot.\n2. **Shore** — two Wide Stairs (the upper one on a Brick 1x2, turned 90°, press **R**) climb onto a stone Block 2x2, where the bridge starts.\n3. **Covered Bridge** — a stone Block 2x2 out in the water is the pier. Two wooden Plate 2x4s, turned 90°, run from the shore over the pier to the rock. Six white Columns stand along the deck, two at each end and two over the pier, and carry two red Gable Roof 2x4s, turned 90° so their ridge runs along the bridge.\n4. **Tower** — three grey Block 2x2s stacked on the far half of the rock, so the bridge lands on open stone. The red Door, turned 90°, faces the bridge; Small Windows look south and north and glow with lamplight at night.\n5. **Lantern** — a dark Plate 2x2 for the gallery, a Lantern that lights up after dark, and a red Hip Roof to match the bridge.\n\nStand it with the first step on the shore and the rest out over the water: the bridge is the only way across.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Rock: 2 Block 2x2, 4 Rock\n- Shore: 2 Wide Stair, 1 Brick 1x2, 1 Block 2x2\n- Covered Bridge: 1 Block 2x2, 2 Plate 2x4, 6 Column, 2 Gable Roof 2x4\n- Tower: 3 Block 2x2, 1 Door, 2 Small Window\n- Lantern: 1 Plate 2x2, 1 Lantern, 1 Hip Roof\n\n30 bricks in all.\n",
